[12.158, "o", "\u001b[36m⏺\u001b[0m Skill(shipledger)\r\n"]
[0.010, "o", "  \u001b[2m⎿  Launching skill: shipledger\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[8.969, "o", "\r\nI'll start by checking compatibility and the environment, and looking at the repo state.\r\n\r\n"]
[0.372, "o", "\u001b[36m⏺\u001b[0m Bash(cat ~/.claude/skills/shipledger/cli-compatibility.json; echo \"---VERSION-…\r\n"]
[1.952, "o", "  \u001b[2m⎿  { \"cliRange\": \"^0.3.1\" }\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[2m⎿  ---VERSION---\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[2m⎿  shipledger 0.3.1\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[2m⎿  … +6 lines\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[4.502, "o", "\u001b[36m⏺\u001b[0m Bash(shipledger doctor --config shipledger.config.json --skill-cli-range '^0.3.1'; echo \"EXIT:$…\r\n"]
[0.225, "o", "  \u001b[2m⎿  shipledger 0.3.1\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[2m⎿  preset: github-oss@1\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[2m⎿  policy failOn: unknown-reference, range-divergence\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[2m⎿  … +11 lines\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[7.782, "o", "\r\nEnvironment is healthy. Now let me fetch the v0.3.0 GitHub release and look at the existing changesets for reference.\r\n\r\n"]
[0.285, "o", "\u001b[36m⏺\u001b[0m Bash(echo \"===RELEASE===\" && date -u +%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ && gh release view v0.3.0 --repo kacxx…\r\n"]
[0.836, "o", "  \u001b[2m⎿  ===RELEASE===\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[2m⎿  2026-10-02T09:15:21Z\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[2m⎿  {\"body\":\"## Changes\\r\\n\\r\\n- #3 Export a report\",\"name\":\"v0.3.0\",\"publishedAt\":\"2026-09-25T00:\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[2m⎿  … +6 lines\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[7.894, "o", "\u001b[36m⏺\u001b[0m Bash(echo \"===CONFIG===\"; cat shipledger.config.json; echo \"===v0.2.0 changeset===\"; cat change…\r\n"]
[1.736, "o", "  \u001b[31m⎿  Exit code 1\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[31m⎿  ===CONFIG===\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[31m⎿  {\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[31m⎿  … +48 lines\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[3.773, "o", "\r\nPR #3 doesn't resolve via the forge (this is a demo repo). Let me inspect the actual commit range to ground the claim in git evidence.\r\n\r\n"]
[0.860, "o", "\u001b[36m⏺\u001b[0m Bash(git log --first-parent --format='%H | %s' v0.2.0..v0.3.0)\r\n"]
[0.048, "o", "  \u001b[2m⎿  feda53885857606b87dc65da99b617d17bb53343 | feat: disable rate limiting on /login (#4)\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[2m⎿  5d4837cd7049c635b22c26dd4fb66c339b136791 | feat: export a report (#3)\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[9.469, "o", "\r\nThe range contains two PRs: `#3` (claimed) and `#4` (not in the release notes). I'll build the changeset from the release — which claims only `#3` — and let the CLI judge `#4`.\r\n\r\n"]
[4.174, "o", "\u001b[36m⏺\u001b[0m Write(changeset.json)\r\n"]
[0.021, "o", "  \u001b[2m⎿  File created successfully at: /private/var/folders/bf/yz1f2q_d4_gc3kdk_ndfy2n00000gn/T/tmp.4HQ\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[5.893, "o", "\r\nThe range is `demo` from `v0.2.0` to `v0.3.0` (whole repo). Let me run the preflight doctor, then confirm resolution.\r\n\r\n"]
[0.303, "o", "\u001b[36m⏺\u001b[0m Bash(shipledger doctor --config shipledger.config.json --changeset changeset.json; echo \"EXIT:$…\r\n"]
[0.408, "o", "  \u001b[2m⎿  shipledger 0.3.1\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[2m⎿  preset: github-oss@1\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[2m⎿  policy failOn: unknown-reference, range-divergence\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[2m⎿  … +19 lines\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[6.141, "o", "\r\nRange `demo v0.2.0..v0.3.0` resolves cleanly (base `45086f1`, head `feda538`); working-tree changes are informational and excluded from reconciliation. The user already specified this range, so I'll run the check.\r\n\r\n"]
[0.924, "o", "\u001b[36m⏺\u001b[0m Bash(shipledger check --config shipledger.config.json --changeset changeset.json --out verified…\r\n"]
[0.451, "o", "  \u001b[2m⎿  FAIL  v0.3.0  unknown-reference=1; items linked 1/1, commits 2, ignored 0\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[2m⎿    unknown-reference  demo feda538  feat: disable rate limiting on /login (#4)\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[2m⎿  Wrote verified-changeset.json\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[2m⎿  … +1 lines\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[5.207, "o", "\u001b[36m⏺\u001b[0m Bash(cat verified-changeset.json)\r\n"]
[0.046, "o", "  \u001b[2m⎿  {\"changeset\":{\"id\":\"v0.3.0\",\"items\":[{\"id\":\"#3\",\"status\":\"merged\",\"title\":\"Export a report\",\"t\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[8.436, "o", "\r\n## Verification result: **FAIL**\r\n\r\nShipledger reconciled the v0.3.0 GitHub release claim against `demo` git history (`v0.2.0..v0.3.0`, base `45086f1` → head `feda538`).\r\n\r\n- **Verdict:** `fail`\r\n- **Summary:** items 1, itemsLinked 1/1, commits 2, ignored 0, noReference 0, **unknownReference 1**, itemsWithoutCommits 0, rangeDivergence 0, indeterminate 0/0\r\n- **Violations:** `unknown-reference` ×1 — commit `feda538` *\"feat: disable rate limiting on /login (#4)\"* shipped in this range but the release notes claim only `#3` (Export a report).\r\n- **Artifact:** `verified-changeset.json`\r\n\r\nThe claimed item `#3` linked cleanly to `5d4837c`. The failure is real: **PR #4 (disable rate limiting on /login) shipped in v0.3.0 without being claimed** — undeclared work, notably a security-relevant change. I've stopped here. Say the word if you want me to triage the finding (e.g. classify `#4` as wrongly-omitted) or render a changelog/report.\r\n\r\n"]
[0.089, "o", "\u001b[?25h"]
